# The Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process
# A quantity pulled back to zero while noise pushes it about, such as the
# velocity of a particle in a fluid (Uhlenbeck and Ornstein, 1930). Its mean
# decays exponentially from the start, at the rate theta, while its variance
# grows to sigma squared over twice theta. Run many times to see both.
wiener w
x'=-theta*x+sigma*w
par theta=1,sigma=0.5
init x=2
@ total=5,dt=0.01,meth=euler
@ xp=t,yp=x,xlo=0,xhi=5,ylo=-1,yhi=3
done
